{\f1\fs16\cf5\b SECTION 4 \emdash  INSTALLATION SCOPE & SECURITY CERTIFICATES\par}
\par
{\f1\fs17\cf11\b 4.1  Installation Architecture.\b0\f0\fs17\cf11  The installer provides flexible installation paradigms: standard Per-User mode (isolated in AppData, requiring zero administrative rights) and system-wide All-Users mode (residing in Program Files, requiring local elevation).}\par
\par
{\f1\fs17\cf11\b 4.2  Local Publisher Certificate.\b0\f0\fs17\cf11  To protect against binary tampering and prevent false Windows SmartScreen warnings on first run, the installer imports an official publisher certificate into your machine's CurrentUser Trusted Root/Publisher store. This certificate carries zero telemetry, transmits zero telemetry, and serves solely for cryptographic software signature verification.}\par
\par

{\f1\fs16\cf5\b SECTION 5 \emdash  UPDATES & CONTINUOUS SECURITY\par}
\par
{\f1\fs17\cf11\b 5.1  Automatic Security Ingestion.\b0\f0\fs17\cf11  To maintain active defense against zero-day vulnerabilities in the underlying Chromium engine, Ocal Browser is configured to periodically check our official release channels for updated binaries. You consent to the receipt of security patches, stability upgrades, and engine optimizations.}\par
\par
{\f1\fs17\cf11\b 5.2  Feature Evolution.\b0\f0\fs17\cf11  We continuously refine features to support modern Web APIs, privacy shields, and operating system updates. We reserve the right to deprecate legacy protocols or modify features to preserve overall platform security.}\par
\par

